{
  "name": "Draft answers to interested replies with AI and send them after Slack approval",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Draft answers to interested replies with AI and send them after Slack approval\n\n### How it works\nAnswer interested prospects within minutes, with a human in the loop. The trigger adds the conversation ID to every interested reply. The workflow reads the whole thread and asks your own AI model for a short, plain answer that proposes a next step with the calendar link from Settings. Slack shows the draft with Send and Don't send buttons and waits. Only Send sends the answer from Argorant, in the same thread. Don't send ends the run and nothing goes out.\n\nArgorant replies are free. Your model provider bills its own usage.\n\n### Setup\n1. Install the community node **n8n-nodes-argorant** (tested with 0.3.0 on n8n 2.46.6): Settings > Community nodes > Install. Guide: https://github.com/argorant/n8n-nodes-argorant\n2. Add an **Argorant API** credential with a key from Argorant (Settings, API keys).\n3. Activate the trigger with your Argorant credential. Argorant webhooks come with the Pro plan, and your n8n needs a public HTTPS address.\n4. Put your name and calendar link into **Settings**.\n5. Pick a chat model in **Chat model** (any chat model node works).\n6. Add a Slack credential and the channel or user in **Ask for approval in Slack**.\n\n### Customization\nChange the tone in **Draft the answer**, or approve by email with the send and wait operation of an email node.",
        "height": 687,
        "width": 520,
        "color": 1
      },
      "id": "0ad80733-a5fb-4291-9874-f5e57c329ce6",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -620,
        -360
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Draft\nYour own model writes from the whole thread. Any chat model node works.",
